+          //
+          // The extent is a bounding range in tiled address space, so the bytes
+          // between the resolved tiles belong to pixels outside the resolve
+          // rect. Copying the whole extent back pushes whatever the host buffer
+          // holds there - zeros for pages the guest never wrote - over the
+          // guest's own data, which is why a game resolving less than the full
